            <div xml:id="d61-a1">

                <pb facs="0144" n="24" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg24"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of State to
                        Minister Collier.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-07-02"><hi rendition="#small-caps">July</hi> 2,
                        1905</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have learned with deep regret,
                    through your excellency’s courteous letter of yesterday, of the unexpected death
                    of Mr. John Hay, the United States Secretary of State, of which misfortune I had
                    been acquainted by telegraph.</p>
                <p>In declaring to your excellency my profound grief for so grievous a loss which
                    has been sustained by your excellency and by the American Government, I wish in
                    the name of His Majesty’s Government and in my own name to express heartfelt
                    sorrow.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Sanchez Roman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
